t hard-codes USD instead of using the configured currency could pass.). Tighten the test so it asserts what the criterion says."},{"check":"test-proof","frames":[],"message":"AC-14.1: its test AC_14_1_GeneratedPlanShowsQuantityCostEnergyAndStatus does not prove the criterion (The test only checks that numbers occur in the Pen 41 row; it does not assert that they are displayed as planned quantity, per-animal quantity, cost, and energy, or that the planned quantity is the rate multiplied by the animal count.). Tighten the test so it asserts what the criterion says."},{"check":"test-proof","frames":[],"message":"AC-15.1: its test AC_15_1_ShowsReconciliationFlagAndDifferenceFromPlanTotal does not prove the criterion (The test accepts any mismatch/reconciliation-related text and any occurrence of 400, without asserting an allocation-reconciliation flag and its associated difference.). Tighten the test so it asserts what the criterion says."},{"check":"test-proof","frames":[],"message":"AC-15.2: its test AC_15_2_NamesLotWithoutAllocationAndDoesNotShowPlanSaved does not prove the criterion (The test only excludes a “plan saved” phrase, so a plan could still appear as a saved record or status without that wording.). Tighten the test so it asserts what the criterion says."},{"check":"test-proof","frames":[],"message":"AC-16.1: its test AC_16_1_EventDetailShowsPlannedActualVarianceCostEnergyConsumptionAndStatus does not prove the criterion (The optional `openDetailIfAny` at line 526 can skip opening details, and the test does not distinguish the inventory-consumption value from the identical actual-quantity value.). Tighten the test so it asserts what the criterion says."},{"check":"test-proof","frames":[],"message":"AC-16.2: its test AC_16_2_EventDetailShowsEachLotsReturnedActualAllocationAndEventCost does not prove the criterion (The fixture at lines 531–538 has only two lots despite “each” requiring at least three, and the optional detail navigation can be skipped while the event cost is checked page-wide.). Tighten the test so it asserts what the criterion says."},{"check":"test-proof","frames":[],"message":"AC-16.3: its test AC_16_3_EachEventShowsCostAtItsOwnSavedUnitCost does not prove the criterion (The test returns different cost snapshots at lines 553–557 but never changes an ingredient's unit cost after the first save, so it does not set up the criterion's changed-cost scenario.). Tighten the test so it asserts what the criterion says."},{"check":"test-proof","frames":[],"message":"AC-16.4: its test AC_16_4_ShowsInventoryDecrementAndWastageAdjustedConsumptionSeparately does not prove the criterion (The optional `openDetailIfAny` at line 582 can skip opening the event detail screen, so the assertions could be satisfied by a non-detail view.). Tighten the test so it asserts what the criterion says."},{"check":"test-proof","frames":[],"message":"AC-1.2: its test AC_1_2_ShowsSameControlsInTwoSessions does not prove the criterion (It renders each screen twice sequentially in the same browser context, so it does not compare controls across two independent browser sessions.). Tighten the test so it asserts what the criterion says."},{"check":"test-proof","frames":[],"message":"AC-3.1: its test does not prove the criterion (Both mapping tests verify lot-to-pen names, capacity, and animal count, but do not assert that the displayed association identifies the PO line and numeric pen ID.). Tighten the test so it asserts what the criterion says."},{"check":"test-proof","frames":[],"message":"AC-6.1: its test AC_6_1_ShowsTargetSelectedByLotSpecificOrYardConfiguration does not prove the criterion (The fixtures cover Lot and Yard forecast sources but omit the procurement-target case, so that target-selection case could be broken without failing the test.). Tighten the test so it asserts what the criterion says."},{"check":"test-proof","frames":[],"message":"AC-8.1: its test AC_8_1_ShowsEveryInventoryItemWithDetailsAndStockTotals does not prove the criterion (The generic `lb` assertion can be satisfied by quantity or stock labels even if an item's unit-of-measure value is not displayed.). Tighten the test so it asserts what the criterion says."},{"check":"test-proof","frames":[],"message":"AC-8.2: its test AC_8_2_ShowsReturnedItemWithSubmittedValuesAfterCreate does not prove the criterion (The mock echoes submitted fields and the display assertion compares against that echoed object, so a locally rendered submission could pass; it also never asserts that the submitted category is Protein.). Tighten the test so it asserts what the criterion says."},{"check":"test-proof","frames":[],"message":"AC-24.1: its test AC_24_1_ShowsEveryDashboardMeasureAndMarksBestAndWorstLots does not prove the criterion (Lines 106–117 check unlabelled page-wide numbers but omit active-lot, active-pen, and daily-delivery measures, so assert each requested measure with its label or dashboard region and its response value.). Tighten the test so it asserts what the criterion says."},{"check":"test-proof","frames":[],"message":"AC-26.1: its test AC_26_1_ShowsReturnedLotsWithAdgFcrAndCostOfGainColumns does not prove the criterion (The suite never changes the date-range filter, and lines 343–347 only check dates from the unfixed default request; add a fixed-date range selection and assert its selected values and matching rows.). Tighten the test so it asserts what the criterion says."},{"check":"test-proof","frames":[],"message":"AC-26.2: its test does not prove the criterion (The two tests change sex, lot, and pen but not date range or breed, so add changed-date-range and changed-breed cases that assert the selected values and returned matching rows.). Tighten the test so it asserts what the criterion says."},{"check":"test-proof","frames":[],"message":"AC-27.1: its test AC_27_1_ExportsCsvForTheDisplayedScope does not prove the criterion (Lines 478–500 verify scope on the request URL but inspect only the lot name and sex in a captured blob, so assert every displayed row field and all selected scope metadata in the downloaded CSV using a fixed test date.). Tighten the test so it asserts what the criterion says."},{"check":"test-proof","frames":[],"message":"AC-27.2: its test AC_27_2_ExportsPdfForTheDisplayedScope does not prove the criterion (The PDF mock returns only a constant marker and the test never inspects PDF contents, so provide a content-bearing PDF fixture and assert that the downloaded file contains the displayed results and selected scope.). Tighten the test so it asserts what the criterion says."},{"check":"test-proof","frames":[],"message":"AC-28.1: its test AC_28_1_ShowsYardSummaryTotalsFromSummaryResponse does not prove the criterion (The overview and summary fixtures reuse 232, 3.07, and 1.37, so the page-wide checks can pass if summary values are omitted; use distinct overview values and assert all four totals in the summary region.). Tighten the test so it asserts what the criterion says."},{"check":"test-proof","frames":[],"message":"AC-29.1: its test AC_29_1_ShowsRepresentativeSampleRecordsOfEveryKind does not prove the criterion (The page-wide checks in lines 149–166 can count overview lots and pens or repeated text such as “Pen 14” and “North Yard Grower” instead of records in each category, so assert identifying fields within each record’s row or region.). Tighten the test so it asserts what the criterion says."},{"check":"test-proof","frames":[],"message":"AC-17.2: its test AC_17_2_AdjustFormShowsEditableQuantitiesPenAndRation does not prove the criterion (It requires only one editable field matching broad quantity/rate/allocation labels, so a form without editable future-plan quantity fields could pass.). Tighten the test so it asserts what the criterion says."},{"check":"test-proof","frames":[],"message":"AC-19.1: its test AC_19_1_WeightHistoryListsRecordsInTimeOrderWithAllColumns does not prove the criterion (The test skips the returned zero weight-gain value for the